iced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\" (utility-credit), so investment-grade issuers can borrow.\n- **Plans are growing.** 2027 capex is up 18% at Pellham and 12% at Norvane, mostly substations and transformers (utility-capex-2027).\n- **Equity is the weak point.** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity raise after demand fell short (pellham-offering). Without that equity, funding the plan would need more debt, which strains leverage and credit ratings. The sources don't give leverage or rating data, so I can't say how much room there is.\n- **Pellham is cutting.** It said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering). That suggests debt alone won't cover its plan.\n\n**By company:**\n- **Norvane** (smaller increase, proven debt access) looks able to fund its plan mostly with debt.\n- **Pellham** (larger increase, failed equity raise) looks constrained, even though debt is technically available.\n\n**Gaps.** The sources don't include the size of the funding gap, current leverage or rating headroom, or Pellham's debt-issuance plans. The conclusion rests on the Norvane deal and Pellham's own cutbacks. The equity-market question is covered by sibling node n6.","ttft_ms":2446,"type":"result","duration_ms":24931,"uuid":"2088cdfc-6572-495d-8741-a5b6471505c3","ttft_stream_ms":1149,"time_to_request_ms":72,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":15,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_la